  "2026-09-02T11:43:08.623Z","harness:codex","Temporary-directory acceptance: a fresh Git/npm project was initialized with the branch CLI, qa-context was created and closed, pm-changelog 2026.9.2 was installed through pm package install, and changelog generation under UTC, Europe/Vienna, and America/Los_Angeles produced byte-identical JSON. The untagged package version heading was 2099.1.2 with no fabricated date and contained qa-context. The first assertion expected Unreleased, which was stricter than the actual --release-version-from-package contract; the corrected contract assertion passed. Temporary data was removed."
  "2026-09-02T12:20:48.192Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review implementation: authoritative append state now survives projection-invalidation contention without retrying the immutable append; path-like stream IDs are rejected before indexed validation; signal snapshots reject blank or duplicate candidate IDs before serialization; SDK init preserves nonblank PM_PATH as an explicit tracker target; timestamp failures use the canonical history_timestamp_invalid envelope while lossless trailing-zero fractions remain accepted; owned lock release outlasts the stale-cleanup threshold and performs a final token ownership check; history override fixtures now contain all lock artifacts within their temporary tracker. Focused regression verification passed 7 files / 155 tests."
  "2026-09-02T12:38:18.597Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review correction evidence: authoritative history append now executes at most once when post-append index invalidation is contended; candidate snapshots reject blank or duplicate IDs before persistence and their digest is anchored against the production serializer; path-like stream IDs are rejected before indexed lookup without provoking rebuild; invalid history timestamp precision uses the stable history_timestamp_invalid taxonomy while accepting only zero-valued sub-millisecond tails; stale lock release waits through the full cleanup-gate lease and removes its lock only after ownership re-verification; SDK init honors explicit PM_PATH without changing active-host cwd discovery; history override tests keep lock artifacts inside their sandbox. Focused suites passed, TypeScript and ESLint passed, and the PM-linked repo-wide coverage gate passed at exactly 61,220/61,220 statements, 46,255/46,255 branches, 12,739/12,739 functions, and 58,924/58,924 lines."
  "2026-09-02T12:39:06.786Z","harness:codex","Static-gate note: the first post-review pnpm quality:static run passed ESLint, both zero-duplication checks, build, contract snapshots, and generated capability surfaces, then correctly failed because the new stable history_timestamp_invalid code made the generated error-code catalog stale. Refreshing that generated contract before rerunning the complete gate."
  "2026-09-02T12:39:57.010Z","harness:codex","Static-gate note: after refreshing the generated error-code catalog, the second complete run passed lint, duplication, and build, then correctly detected the corresponding full contract fixture drift. Refreshing the intentional generated contract snapshot before the final complete rerun."
  "2026-09-02T12:49:49.138Z","harness:codex","Final static evidence: after refreshing the generated error-code catalog and contract fixture and restoring runtime.ts to the repository's intentional compact public-surface layout, the complete CI-mode pnpm quality:static gate passed. It verified ESLint, zero duplicated chunks, build, generated contracts, 100% source/export/member docstrings, file/directory/complexity limits, package boundaries, SDK parity, replication, grammar, refusal closure, token budgets, MCP deprecation dispositions, context quality, graph composition, and record integrity."
  "2026-09-02T13:12:43.467Z","harness:codex","Investigation note: final exact-head Cubic and CodeRabbit reviews found a TOCTOU risk in the unguarded release fallback, missing abandoned pending-marker recovery, Windows Start-Process argument-boundary loss, duplicate recency fingerprint work, and four test-strength issues. Reopening the canonical item and implementing all valid findings with focused negative controls before another exact-head review round."
  "2026-09-02T13:31:34.488Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review remediation evidence: hardened lock cleanup against live cleanup-gate ownership; added behavioral publication-race coverage for committed invalidations and temporary artifact cleanup; recovered abandoned pending invalidations under the invalidation lock; preserved Windows verifier arguments and exit codes through direct PowerShell invocation; reused the authoritative context-snapshot fingerprint; expanded RFC3339 branch, scale-manifest negative-control, and canonical digest-helper coverage. Focused 170-test review suite passed, the added event-index race test passed, and the canonical repository coverage gate passed with exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines."
  "2026-09-02T13:38:19.432Z","harness:codex","Final local gate evidence: CI=1 PM_NON_INTERACTIVE=1 pnpm quality:static passed end-to-end after the exact-head review fixes, including ESLint with zero warnings, zero jscpd clones, build/typecheck, generated contract and SDK surface freshness, package boundary and SDK parity, token/transport floors, command grammar, flag parity, refusal closure, repository assurance, graph composition, tracker context quality, and append-only record integrity."
  "2026-09-02T14:02:11.484Z","harness:codex","Cubic recurrence remediation: pending event-index invalidation markers now encode their writer PID. Recovery removes only legacy or OS-confirmed-dead owners, conservatively retains live, permission-denied, malformed-error, and otherwise unverifiable owners, and forces rebuild/index reads onto safe refusal or authoritative fallback while a writer can still complete after TTL takeover. Behavioral tests cover live, indeterminate, permission-denied, dead, publication-race, and indexed-query paths. Focused event-index tests, ESLint, TypeScript, and canonical repo-wide exact 100/100/100/100 coverage pass."
  "2026-09-02T14:08:58.667Z","harness:codex","Final recurrence gate evidence: CI=1 PM_NON_INTERACTIVE=1 pnpm quality:static passed after owner-bound pending invalidations, including zero ESLint warnings, zero jscpd clones, build/typecheck, generated contracts/surfaces, package and SDK parity, token and transport floors, graph composition, tracker context quality, and append-only history integrity."
  "2026-09-02T14:53:09.004Z","harness:codex","Terminal paginated-review remediation: event-index pending owners now carry PID, process-start identity, and creation time; PID reuse is rejected by identity mismatch and unavailable identity is retained only within a bounded TTL-derived grace period. Context snapshots reject non-string history_op before persistence. Init invocation state uses one unique-symbol constant owned by init.ts, a symbol index signature, and runtime string validation without exceeding the 120-file SDK cap. Assertions now prove non-empty init guidance, declaration-over-inference, and actual DatabaseSync assignment triggers. Focused 141-test suite and canonical exact 100/100/100/100 coverage pass."
  "2026-09-02T15:07:45.170Z","harness:codex","Final hosted-review hardening evidence: substantive-history recency now rejects non-string history operation provenance; CLI init shares one typed invocation-CWD symbol and validates its untrusted value; init acceptance proves actionable next_steps are non-empty; the history classifier negative control uses a declared substantive maintenance-only update; and the DatabaseSync replication test exercises a real constructor assignment. Pending history-index invalidations now bind PID ownership to process-start identity, expire unverifiable owners under a bounded grace period, and reject PID reuse; real /proc-unavailable fallback is covered. The focused regression suite passed 73/73. The canonical repository coverage gate passed exact 100/100/100/100 after these changes. CI=1 PM_NON_INTERACTIVE=1 pnpm quality:static passed the complete ESLint, zero-clone, build, contract, docstring, repository assurance, package/SDK parity, surface replication, grammar, refusal, agent-token, MCP, tracker-context, SDK cost, graph-composition, and record-integrity chain."
  "2026-09-02T15:31:01.636Z","harness:codex","Investigation note: exact head b0179f263 received one Cubic and six CodeRabbit threads after all hosted checks passed. Verifying PID-domain validation, malformed patch classification, post-commit invalidation containment, shared lock ownership predicates, symbol typing against the installed compiler, exact delivered IDs, test isolation cost, and explicit unsupported-host skips before changing code."
  "2026-09-02T16:12:18.785Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review hardening evidence: accepted and implemented fail-closed malformed update patch classification, strict positive safe-integer PID validation before process probes, canonical lock-owner predicate reuse, exact active-host delivery receipt assertions, explicit Vitest skips on hosts without process-start identity, and post-commit history append durability across projection close/invalidation/marker-publication failures. Pre-commit append and lock failures still reject. Focused regression suite passed 96/96 before the additional coverage controls; TypeScript no-emit compilation passed. The repo-wide linked coverage gate correctly failed twice while new branches or displaced marker-cleanup callbacks were not explicit, then passed after direct negative controls; final result is exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. The shared INIT_INVOCATION_CWD unique-symbol review suggestion is disproven by the installed TypeScript compiler and the giant invalidation recovery test remains intentionally consolidated to reuse one isolated tracker while keeping each race assertion localized."
  "2026-09-02T16:42:33.298Z","harness:codex","Investigation note: exact head fbe6d6e4b received three Cubic and four CodeRabbit threads after all hosted checks passed. Verifying duplicate pending-marker cleanup findings, public SDK recency-evidence normalization, portable reused-PID coverage, recomputed snapshot fingerprints, bounded test-run projection retention, and the exact failed-run count before edits."
  "2026-09-02T16:48:53.122Z","harness:codex","Evidence correction: the 2026-09-02 16:12 UTC comment understated the final coverage convergence count. Four consecutive coverage runs failed before test-local-mtkan1uz-esga7j passed: test-local-mtk9lk0c-3aidbi exposed the committed-index fallback catch; test-local-mtk9wham-pnwenk exposed the fallback marker rename error; test-local-mtka5c20-xg4e94 exposed post-commit database-close handling; and test-local-mtkady19-uujn97 exposed the absent-index path. This append-only correction preserves the original event while stating the complete live run history."
  "2026-09-02T17:03:40.811Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review remediation evidence: the public item relevance builder now validates provenance and canonicalizes supplied absolute recency coordinates before ranking or disclosure; valid offsets round-trip to UTC and malformed values fail at the SDK boundary. The event-index lock-contention fallback removes its pending invalidation marker after authoritative history commits even when marker publication fails, while a direct cleanup-denied negative control proves cleanup remains best effort without losing the append. Reused-PID recovery now uses a localized procfs fixture and snapshot parser shape controls recompute their fingerprints. The focused 59-test regression set passed. The final repository run passed all 8,305 tests at exactly 61,248/61,248 statements, 46,272/46,272 branches, 12,742/12,742 functions, and 58,951/58,951 lines."
  "2026-09-02T17:31:51.779Z","harness:codex","Canonical final coverage receipt: pm-linked run test-local-mtkdhg9c-ih5h9k executed linked test index 2 (node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage) against exact source head 3897d1757e1fc17b9a7823124eb5946ba01d1e70 and passed. The run covered all 8,305 tests with exact 61,248/61,248 statements, 46,272/46,272 branches, 12,742/12,742 functions, and 58,951/58,951 lines. This machine-addressable test_run_track event is the canonical receipt for the closure totals requested by Cubic; the bounded item projection may rotate older entries while immutable history retains every test-run event."
