  "2026-09-02T18:26:08.692Z","harness:codex","Investigation note: final Cubic review correctly identified that rejection payload and failure state are distinct in JavaScript, so Promise.reject(undefined) could bypass current sentinel checks. It also correctly requested that actual_result lead with the primary substantive-recency outcome. Adding explicit failure flags plus undefined-rejection negative controls, then restoring outcome-first closure wording through pm."
  "2026-09-02T18:28:14.533Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: replaced error-value sentinels with explicit feedbackFailed and touchFailed state so Promise.reject(undefined) remains an observable failure while durable touches are still attempted. Added negative controls for undefined feedback and touch rejections. Focused context-eval suite passed 6/6; pnpm exec tsc --noEmit and focused ESLint both passed."
